            <ArticleTitle>Loin Pain Haematuria Syndrome - A Narrative Review of Pain Management Strategies.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>78-85</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.3344/kjp.2016.29.2.78</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Loin pain haematuria syndrome (LPHS) is an uncommon clinical entity that has divided renal physicians, pain practitioners, and even psychiatrists since its initial description. A relative paucity of data exists regarding the condition, with best practice guidelines lacking amid the existing threads of anecdotal experiences and variable follow-up observations. The aim of this article was to review the cumulative published experience of pain relief strategies for LPHS.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
